// Virtual Memory Address Translation
VIRTUAL_ADDRESS = (page_number, offset)

FUNCTION translate(virtual_address):
    page_number = virtual_address / PAGE_SIZE
    offset = virtual_address % PAGE_SIZE

    IF page_table[page_number].present == TRUE:
        frame_number = page_table[page_number].frame
        physical_address = (frame_number * PAGE_SIZE) + offset
        RETURN physical_address
    ELSE:
        // PAGE FAULT
        LOAD page from disk into a free frame
        UPDATE page_table[page_number]
        RETRY translation

// Page Replacement Algorithms:
// FIFO: evict oldest page in memory
// LRU: evict least recently used page
// Optimal: evict page not needed for longest time (theoretical)

// FCFS (First Come First Served)
Queue: P1(bt=24), P2(bt=3), P3(bt=3)
Execution: P1 → P2 → P3
Avg Waiting Time = (0 + 24 + 27) / 3 = 17ms  ← convoy effect

// SJF (Shortest Job First – non-preemptive)
Queue: P1(bt=6), P2(bt=8), P3(bt=7), P4(bt=3)
Sorted: P4(3) → P1(6) → P3(7) → P2(8)
Avg WT = (0+3+9+16) / 4 = 7ms  ← optimal avg WT

// Round Robin (quantum = 4ms)
Queue: P1(bt=10), P2(bt=6), P3(bt=4)
Execution: P1(4) → P2(4) → P3(4) → P1(4) → P2(2) → P1(2)
// Each process gets a fixed time slice; fair but more overhead

// Priority Scheduling
Process with highest priority runs first
If equal priority → use FCFS as tiebreaker
Risk: Starvation (low priority never runs) → solved by Aging

// TCP 3-Way Handshake
CLIENT → SERVER: SYN (seq=x)          // 'I want to connect'
SERVER → CLIENT: SYN-ACK (seq=y, ack=x+1)  // 'OK, I'm ready'
CLIENT → SERVER: ACK (ack=y+1)        // 'Connection established'

// TCP Data Transfer
CLIENT → SERVER: DATA (seq=1)
SERVER → CLIENT: ACK (ack=2)          // 'Got it, send next'
CLIENT → SERVER: DATA (seq=2)
// If no ACK received → CLIENT retransmits

// UDP (no handshake)
CLIENT → SERVER: SEND packet          // fire and forget
CLIENT → SERVER: SEND packet          // no guarantee of delivery
// No ACK, no retransmission

// TCP Teardown: 4-way FIN handshake
CLIENT → SERVER: FIN
SERVER → CLIENT: ACK
SERVER → CLIENT: FIN
CLIENT → SERVER: ACK

